  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Proposed loft conversion to a residential mid terrace first floor flat. Erection of a rear dormer & L-Shape Dormer to the existing roof space of the first floor flat. \n\n3No. Velux windows to the front elevation roof. 2No. Casements windows to the rear elevation of the rear dormer. \n\nFlat roof dormer to be covered in three layer high performance roofing felt.\n\nDormer to be clad in plain tiles that are to match the existing roof tiles.\n\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:-34.6pt;margin-bottom:\r\n12.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;The application proposal which aims to create a\r\nfamily sized flat would create cramped, substandard accommodation by way of the\r\noverall gross internal floor area for a three-bedroom, 4-person, 2 storey\r\ndwelling significantly failing to meet the minimum internal space standards, a\r\ndouble-bedroom which falls short of the required standard, which has a&amp;nbsp; compromised ceiling height and outlook, and\r\nwithout any external amenity space which overall would create sub-standard,\r\npoor quality accommodation for a family sized flat which is contrary to policies\r\n56 and 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024) and Policy D6 of the London Plan.&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
